From: Petr Stetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Subject: [PATCH] ath12k: print the masked debug messages with dev_info

__ath12k_dbg() prints with dev_dbg(), which is compiled out on the
Freedom image (no CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG at run time, no -DDEBUG), so the
debug_mask bits select messages that never appear. Print the messages
that pass the debug_mask gate with dev_info(), so that the EAPOL, PEER
and MLME classes reach the kernel log. The mask gate and the branch
without a device stay as they are.

Throwaway debug patch for the Freedom build, never merged.

Assisted-by: claude:sonnet-5-5
Signed-off-by: Petr Stetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/debug.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/debug.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/debug.c
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@
 
 	if (mask & ath12k_debug_mask) {
 		if (ab)
-			dev_dbg(ab->dev, "%pV", &vaf);
+			dev_info(ab->dev, "%pV", &vaf);
 		else
 			pr_info("ath12k: %pV", &vaf);
 	}
-- 
